        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Brewton%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named after early settler Benjamin Bruton, who helped establish it alongside Fort Crawford.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/east-brewton/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fort Crawford, built to protect settlers, is listed on the Alabama Register of Landmarks and Heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/east-brewton/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "East Brewton lies near the site of the Battle of Murder Creek, fought shortly after the 1813 Fort Mims Massacre.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/east-brewton/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "During the Battle of Murder Creek, a lieutenant under Andrew Jackson's command defeated a band of Creek Indians.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/east-brewton/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
